Bootstrapping uses founder resources and operating cash; cash management protects survival before external funding.|A startup delays nonessential spending to reach customer validation.|Growth without funding discipline guarantees survival?|No|Yes|Only in software
Startup plans link customer adoption, monetisation, costs, milestones, and cash needs.|User growth rises while contribution remains negative.|A complete plan includes…?|Unit economics and funding gaps|Only user counts|Only total market size
Gross burn measures cash spending; net burn subtracts cash inflows; runway compares usable cash with net burn.|Cash ₹120 and constant monthly net burn ₹10 imply 12 months.|Runway assumes burn and funding remain…?|As modelled|Guaranteed forever|Irrelevant
Product-market fit concerns durable demand; financing milestones reduce uncertainty with evidence.|A pilot shows repeat usage and paying-customer retention.|A download spike alone proves durable fit?|No|Yes|Only after advertising
Angel, seed, VC, and growth funding differ in stage, risk, investor roles, and terms.|Early investors fund validation; later rounds may fund scaling.|Round names guarantee identical rights?|No|Yes|Only domestically
Cap tables track ownership and potential dilution from shares and awards.|100 existing shares plus 25 new shares leaves existing holders at 80%.|Existing holders' percentage becomes…?|80%|75%|100%
Post-money equals pre-money plus new investment under a simple priced-round model.|Pre-money ₹80 plus investment ₹20 gives ₹100 post-money and 20% new ownership.|New investor ownership is…?|20%|25%|80%
Convertible notes and SAFE-type instruments defer or condition equity conversion; caps, discounts, and legal terms differ.|A valuation cap may determine conversion price rather than the next round's headline value.|A cap guarantees the company's current valuation?|No|Yes|Only for SAFEs
Term sheets describe economic and control terms, with binding status varying by clause and law.|The same headline valuation can accompany different preference and veto rights.|Compare valuation alone?|No|Yes|Only at seed stage
Liquidation preferences and participation determine exit distributions under agreed terms.|A 1× nonparticipating investor chooses preference or conversion as specified.|Ownership percentage alone always determines exit payout?|No|Yes|Only for founders
Anti-dilution adjusts qualifying conversion terms after lower-priced rounds; full-ratchet and weighted-average approaches differ.|A down round activates an agreed price adjustment.|It necessarily protects every shareholder equally?|No|Yes|Only if approved
Vesting earns ownership over time or milestones; options grant conditional share-purchase rights.|A four-year vesting plan limits unearned founder ownership on early departure.|Unvested awards always equal unrestricted shares?|No|Yes|Only for employees
Venture debt adds repayment obligations to high-uncertainty equity-backed businesses.|Debt extends runway but creates interest, covenants, and maturity risk.|It replaces equity risk without new obligations?|No|Yes|Only for funded startups
Fundraising strategy matches milestones, runway, investor fit, disclosures, and negotiation timing.|Starting outreach shortly before cash exhaustion reduces negotiating flexibility.|Best preparation includes…?|Evidence, cash scenarios, and realistic timelines|Only a pitch logo|Only a valuation target
SaaS, marketplace, consumer, and fintech models require different acquisition, retention, transaction, and risk metrics.|Marketplace GMV ₹100 at 10% take rate yields ₹10 revenue before costs.|GMV necessarily equals revenue?|No|Yes|Only online
Down rounds, bridges, and recapitalisations trade immediate funding against dilution, terms, and viability.|A bridge funds three months without resolving the structural cash gap.|More funding alone proves a viable business?|No|Yes|Only from existing investors
Exit routes include sale, listing, and other liquidity events; waterfalls apply contractual claims and costs.|Sale proceeds first meet debt and preference terms before common distribution.|Founders receive headline sale value times ownership automatically?|No|Yes|Only after taxes
